From 174c4cfc72aac1291ec816c422cd7b6970e83e3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aliosa27 <aliosa27@aliosa27.me>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:41:45 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] Drop AT+PING and AT+IPERF2 to free ~6 KB of SRAM; fix
 MAC wrap

- SYS_ATCMD_NETTEST (project_config.h, default 0) gates both commands,
  so lwIP ping and lwiperf are no longer linked
- webui_page.h: overview no longer wraps the last MAC character
---
 NOTES.md                 |  3 +-
 project/atcmd.c          |  4 +-
 project/project_config.h |  1 +
 project/webui_page.h     | 84 ++++++++++++++++++++--------------------
 4 files changed, 47 insertions(+), 45 deletions(-)

diff --git a/NOTES.md b/NOTES.md
index 504e156..50f81f1 100644
--- a/NOTES.md
+++ b/NOTES.md
@@ -12,7 +12,8 @@ Taixin TXW8301 (TXW4002A, C-SKY CK803) HaLow wireless-bridge (WNB) firmware SDK
 
 ## Hard constraints
 
-- **Most RAM goes to the image.** The boot ROM copies the whole image into SRAM (`0x20001000`) and runs it there, so every byte of code or const data (including the embedded web page) costs RAM. What is left above the image is the pool: 60 KB system heap, 64 KB WiFi RX buffer, and the SKB pool (whatever remains, ~178 KB without the web UI). Growing the image shrinks the SKB pool and can hurt bridge throughput. Use the heap sparingly and prefer short-lived allocations.
+- **Most RAM goes to the image.** The boot ROM copies the whole image into SRAM (`0x20001000`) and runs it there, so every byte of code or const data (including the embedded web page) costs RAM. What is left above the image is the pool: 60 KB system heap, 64 KB WiFi RX buffer, and the SKB pool (whatever remains, ~178 KB without the web UI). Growing the image shrinks the SKB pool and can hurt bridge throughput. Builds about 4 KB bigger than the current one did not boot (see Parked ideas). Use the heap sparingly and prefer short-lived allocations.
+- **Size budget.** In `project.map`, see "Image component sizes" and the totals at the end. The closed `liblmac` and `libwifi` take ~245 KB, and the web UI ~60 KB. Unused includes and functions cost nothing: the build uses `-Os` with `--gc-sections`. To free space, remove features. `SYS_ATCMD_NETTEST=0` (`project_config.h`) drops `AT+PING` and `AT+IPERF2`, about 6 KB (lwIP ping and lwiperf).
 - **Flash is 1 MB** (`device.c`). OTA slots are at `0x00000` and `0x80000`. The last four 4 KB sectors are config: `webcfg` A/B at `0xFC000`/`0xFD000`, then `syscfg` A/B at `0xFE000`/`0xFF000`. The OTA image size limit is therefore `0x7C000` bytes, enforced in `webui.c` (`WEBUI_FW_MAX`).
 - **`struct sys_config` (`syscfg.h`) must not change size.** syscfg checks the size, so changing it makes every upgraded device fall back to factory defaults. Put new persistent data in a separate syscfg region instead: map its name in `syscfg_info_get()` (`device.c`) and use `syscfg_read`/`syscfg_write`. Never call `syscfg_init()` a second time, because it re-creates the library's global mutex.
 - **lwIP:** `LWIP_SO_RCVTIMEO`/`SO_SNDTIMEO` are 0, and closed libraries share lwIP struct layouts, so do not change `lwipopts.h`. Use `lwip_select()` with a timeout before socket I/O. `MEMP_NUM_NETCONN` is only 6.
